#: contents/ui/config/configCommand.qml:139
msgid ""
"Every default command below starts with {engine}, which is replaced by the "
"engine command. Use docker, podman, nerdctl, a full path, or something like "
"“sudo docker”. Picking a preset also fills in how the service is started and "
"stopped; the usual setup for your distribution is the first entry. Podman "
"support is experimental."
msgstr ""

#: contents/ui/config/configCommand.qml:145
msgid ""
"Commands may contain placeholders that are substituted before the command "
"runs: {engine} the engine command, {id} short container id, {name} container "
"name (quoted), {image} image reference (quoted), {shell} shell binary, "
"{tail} number of log lines, {project} compose project name, {file} compose "
"file path. Subshells such as $(...) work too."
msgstr ""

#: contents/ui/config/configCommand.qml:153
msgid "Reading"
msgstr ""

#: contents/ui/config/configCommand.qml:160
msgid ""
"Docker is considered running when the check command exits with status 0. The "
"default asks the daemon directly, so it also works for rootless Docker, "
"remote contexts and podman. A command that prints 'inactive' or 'failed' is "
"treated as down even on a zero exit."
msgstr ""

